# The third brief, and the one that needed a phase change to exist.
#
# Crude arrives ambient and a column will not separate anything below the
# scorching band, so two preheaters lift it two bands each. The column then
# sends the light fraction off the top as a *vapour* -- a different domain, a
# different colour of wire, and a fraction that will not plug into the outlet
# the middle fraction goes to. That is what the condenser is for, and it is why
# there is a second pump drawing cold water and a heat sink taking the heat
# straight back out again.
#
# The reactor is at 60% because that is very nearly what three heat wires
# actually swallow. At 100% it would produce the same light and middle and
# waste 400 heat a tick doing it.

machine "Refinery Unit"
brief distil

pump      P1  at 0,0   draws crude
preheater PH1 at 4,0
preheater PH2 at 9,0
column    CO1 at 14,0  stages 2
condenser CD1 at 19,0
outlet    O1  at 19,5
skip      SK1 at 19,8

pump      P2  at 24,0
radiator  RD1 at 24,3

reactor   R1  at 4,4   throttle 42

wire P1.water -> PH1.in
wire PH1.out -> PH2.in
wire PH2.out -> CO1.feed

wire R1.heat -> PH1.heat
wire R1.heat -> PH2.heat
wire R1.heat -> CO1.heat

wire CO1.light -> CD1.vapour
wire P2.water -> CD1.coolant
wire CD1.out -> O1.liquid
wire CD1.heat -> RD1.heat

wire CO1.middle -> O1.liquid
wire CO1.heavy -> SK1.liquid
